            <h3>&quot;Rewrite&quot; is the most expensive word in software</h3>
            <p>A full rewrite is occasionally the right answer and usually not. It throws away years of accumulated business logic — including the strange-looking rules that turn out to encode something real.</p>
            <p>We look first at what can be kept. If a rewrite genuinely is the cheaper path, we will show you the working that led there rather than simply assert it.</p>
